                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif text-white mt-1">City of Phoenix v. Garretson</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="text-right">
                    <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block">Final Judgment</span>
                    <span class="text-xl font-bold text-emerald-400">~$4,000,000</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
                Light rail construction eliminated access to Jefferson Street. The City appraised the take at $7,000; the jury awarded nearly $3,000,000. <strong class="text-white">Mr. Zeitlin successfully argued the case before the Arizona Supreme Court</strong>, establishing that property owners possess a distinct property right of access to a particular street. Briefs and oral arguments were handled directly by Mr. Zeitlin.
            </p>
        </div>

